{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>I will hear</b> — The poet's words seek a path of prophecy, like: \"I will stand at my watch\" (Habakkuk 2:1), until he sees in a vision that HaShem too will return from Israel, and speak peace upon His people for insipidity, from the root כסיל, like: \"and you are all righteous people\" (Proverbs)."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 85, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:36:05.503519919Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}